    "update_time": 1786863550.0177684,
    "content": {
     "content_type": "text",
     "parts": [
      "Your shape is missing a level. Each matcher entry needs a `hooks` array of hook objects with a `type`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"hooks\": {\n    \"PostToolUse\": [\n      {\n        \"matcher\": \"Edit|Write\",\n        \"hooks\": [\n          { \"type\": \"command\", \"command\": \"node ${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/hooks/log-edit.js\" }\n        ]\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\nOther things to check:\n- Hooks load at session start. Restart the session (or reload plugins) after editing.\n- Run `claude --debug` to see whether the hook matched and what the command printed or exited with.\n- Your script receives the event JSON on **stdin**, not as args. Read it with `process.stdin`.\n\nI'm fairly confident about the nested `hooks` array, but double-check against the current Claude Code hooks docs, since the plugin format has changed between versions."
     ]
    },
